  "caption": "Figure 2: Model architecture. Our model first extracts spatial features of consecutive frames by the frame encoder. To jointly model the temporal relation, we aggregate and interact among the multi-frame features with late-fusion. We randomly pair two frames’ visual representations and pass them into the frame comparator to encode relative motion. Then, we decode the flow from random-paired frames. Through iterative routing, we adopt a dual-layer representation for the flow reconstruction, i.e., outputting the foreground and background flows separately, and composing them with inferred opacity weights. The whole training procedure does not require supervision from any mask annotations.",
